    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d47">

                <pb facs="0150" n="110" xml:id="pg110"/>

                <head>47. Telegram From the Department of State to the
                        Secretary of State, at London<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d47-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1956-08-01T15:08:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 1,
                                1956—3:08 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Tedul 6. Eyes only for the Secretary. You will
                    recall that in commenting upon possible repercussions UK–French military action against Egypt, Rountree mentioned likelihood Israeli would
                    embark upon military campaign thus associating in Arab mind Western intervention
                    with Israeli objectives. You might be interested know in conversation yesterday
                    with Russell, Shiloah<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d47-f2"/> volunteered that if Western powers take any military
                    measures in connection Suez, Israel would insist on participating in them.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Hoover</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d47-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d47-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 974.7301/8–156. Top Secret; Niact. Drafted by Rountree and approved and signed by Hoover.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d47-f2" n="2" xml:id="d47-f2-content">
                <p>The memorandum of this conversation by Russell, dated August 1, is <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ibid</hi>., NEA Files:
                    Lot 59 D 518, Omega—Memos etc. July 1 to August 31, 1956.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
